  "description": "When you have amazing seasonal produce, a frittata is one of the best, and easiest, ways to showcase it. In this version, fresh-picked asparagus and ramps add a juicy green bite that's as pure a celebration of spring as you can get.",
  "notes": "Notes: If you don't have ramps, you can substitute a similar amount of diced leek plus 2 thinly sliced cloves of garlic. Sauté both in oil, like the ramps, until softened.",
